{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LLWHdYopw9eR2Aw6ou8iHG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system that J.C. Liechty runs as a persistent local web app on his own machine (`PUTER`/`gwl-server`). Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, plain-markdown task/project manager.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` with no database and no syncing â€” markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files, etc.) are the source of truth. Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done/cancelled/saved-for-later â†’ restored), each with optional notes.\n\n- **It ships as a self-contained Python web server.** The declared deliverable is `anchor_gui.py` â€” a stdlib-only HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on every request, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently on `http://localhost:8777` under the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown into a \"mission control\" for trio-driven R&D.** Beyond plain tasks, each project is a thin full-width row that launches and tracks work from the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio as durable, server-side jobs â€” with auto-generated, cached project/session summaries (when Â· what-was-asked Â· doc links Â· token+time effort) shown in-place rather than as separate pages.\n\n- **The R&D surface is layered across three designed-and-built versions:**\n  - **v2** â€” a \"truthful memory\" model: one trio run = one *session* (not N file-cards), first-class imported/brownfield history, validated+cached summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), a Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable declare/pin, and an interactive stream-json REPL terminal.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** (built by Foreman 2026-06-12, not yet merged) â€” real **ConPTY** terminals, per-session **git-worktree isolation**, a stacking draggable window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs (plan-set â†’ build), a runnable deliverable **preview** server (OS-assigned port, hard-guarded â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **It is deliberately dependency-minimal.** Python 3.8+ stdlib only, with exactly **one** declared exception â€” optional `pywinpty` (lazy `import winpty`, in `pty_manager.py` only) for the v3 ConPTY terminals, installable as a `pip install .[terminal]` extra and degrading gracefully if absent. `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this rule.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint, and walking the full v2 and v3 R&D surfaces â€” all with model calls stubbed (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`/`fake_claude.py`, `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`) so nothing touches live data â€” then writes a dated report.\n\nIn short: **Anchor is a single-user, single-folder, stdlib-Python productivity dashboard that doubles as a durable control surface for launching and remembering AI-trio R&D work on each of John's projects.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e8f8573-e1d0-4256-a3da-5b9bd92f736a","uuid":"18976c97-1234-4fca-80c8-fd7b5ac7188f","request_id":"req_011CbyRCaj5g8smpszL1HSid"}
